course: dictionary
lesson: 13148
title: Words for people at work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A forester is a person whose job is to look after a forest. Look at the word: forest is the place, and the forester is the person who works there. The clues help you when you meet the word in a sentence.
explain: «The forester planted new oak trees on the hill.» The word planted tells you what a forester does. Ask: what word would fit here? A forester plants trees, so a forester is someone who works with trees and the land.
explain: Foresters also cut trees, protect wildlife and try to stop fires. «The forester warned the campers to put out their fire.» The word warned and the word fire are your clues: a forester wants to keep the forest safe.
explain: Old stories have foresters too. «In the old story, the king's forester caught a poacher hiding in the trees.» A poacher is someone who sneaks into a place to take animals or trees they should not have. The context shows that the forester was a guard, and that is what a forester was in those stories.
fact: A forester is a person whose job is to look after a forest.
fact: Foresters plant trees, cut trees, protect wildlife and prevent fires.
fact: «Forester» is a noun. One is a forester; more than one are foresters.
fact: In old stories, a forester guarded the king's forest from poachers.
fact: The phrase «forest ranger» is used for a similar kind of job, looking after woodland and its wildlife.
exercise: «The forester planted new oak trees on the hill.» What is a forester's job? | To sell wooden toys in a shop | To drive a bus through the town | To bake bread for the king | *To look after a forest
exercise: «The forester warned the campers to put out their fire.» What is the forester trying to prevent? | *A fire spreading through the forest | A cold night | A storm at sea | A camping trip
exercise: In old stories, the king's forester guarded the forest from whom? | Kind farmers | *Poachers | The king | Wild birds
test: Which is the plural of forester? | forests | forestry | *foresters | foreseers
test: «The forester cut down the dead tree to keep the forest healthy.» Why would a forester do this? | *To keep the forest healthy | To make the tree fall on a shed | To make a bird sing | To sell the tree to a shop for firewood in the town
exam: Which phrase best describes a forester? | *Someone who looks after a forest | Someone who sells fish at the market | Someone who cooks for the king | Someone who makes paper in a factory
